The United States on Thursday charged ousted Venezuelan president Nicolas Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores with conspiracy to commit torture, adding to drug trafficking and firearms charges. Prosecutors allege detainees, including US citizens, suffered waterboarding, rape and beatings. The pair remain in US custody following a January military raid.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98c20c5a-c337-11f1-a0bd-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2be2ec58aeeef8ac14d762080f9c1624a8e8fcec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98c20c5a-c337-11f1-a0bd-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2be2ec58aeeef8ac14d762080f9c1624a8e8fcec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf80e6f4-c372-11f1-abc1-b3282e3c2c16</guid><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 23:56:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/98c20c5a-c337-11f1-a0bd-f50f6d982dc3/w:1024/p:16x9/2be2ec58aeeef8ac14d762080f9c1624a8e8fcec.jpg">© Pedro MATTEY, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Fort Hood shooter’s firing squad execution to be livestreamed, Pentagon says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261008-fort-hood-shooter-firing-squad-execution-livestreamed-pentagon</link><description>
